```text
PUBLIC SERVICES COMMITTEE
MINUTES
A meeting of the Public Services Committee was held on Tuesday, June 4, 2024, in Committee
Room 104 and via electronic meeting, starting at 12:00 p.m. Those in attendance were as follows:
COMMITTEE MEMBERS: Scott Roybal. Chairman. Pete Laybourn, Dr. Rinnc, and Tom
Segravc.
AGENDA ITEMS
15.
ORDINANCE 3l READING
Amending Chapter 5.78, Towing and Wrecker Recovery
Operations, of Title 5, Business Licenses and Regulations, of the Municipal Code of the
City of Cheyenne, Wyoming, modifying provisions governing towing and wrecker
recovery operation licensure and the Police Department’s towing and wrecker recovery
operation rotation list.
Mr. Segrave moved to approve on 3 and final reading, seconded by Dr. Rinne. Mr. Segrave
moved to amend by substitute dated June 3, 2024 to include the review of the fee schedule every
four (4) years, seconded by Mr. Laybourn. Motion to amend carried with Mr. Layhourn and Mr.
Segrave voting “YES” and Dr. Rinne voting “NO”.
Main motion, as amended, carried by
unanimous voice vote.
Lieutenant Dan Long, Police Department, provided a staff report and John Brodie, Deputy City
Attorney, provided additional information. Committee member Segrave commented on the item
and Ward III Councilman, Richard Johnson, presented a substitute for consideration.
18.
ORDINANCE
READING
— Amending Sections 1.4.3 Defined Terms and 2.2.6
Temporary Use Approval of the Unified Development Code, adding a minimum of
fourteen days. (SPONSOR-- MR. ROYBAL)
Dr. Rinne moved to approve on 2d reading, seconded by Mr. Segrave. Motion carried by
unanimous voice vote.
Connor White. Planning & Development Department, provided a staff report and Seth Lloyd,
Planning & Development Department, provided additional information.
Chairman Roybal and
committee member Rinne commented on the item.
19.
ORDINANCE
_2nd READING
— Amending Section l.4.4.c Service Uses, Table 5-1
Zoning District Uses, Section 5.7.4 Child Care Uses, and Table 6-2 Required Parking of
the Unified Development Code, changing Child Care Requirements. (SPONSOR
— MR.
ROYBAL)
